    "problem_statement": "Parser line tracking broken for multiline .env files\n\nWhen parsing .env files with multiple lines, the line numbers in the `Original` objects are incorrect. The parser seems to be swapping character position and line number values internally.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom dotenv.parser import parse_stream\nimport io\n\n# Simple multiline .env content\ncontent = \"a=b\\nc=d\"\nresult = list(parse_stream(io.StringIO(content)))\n\n# Check the line numbers\nprint(\"First binding line:\", result[0].original.line)  # Should be 1\nprint(\"Second binding line:\", result[1].original.line)  # Should be 2\n\n# Expected: First binding line: 1, Second binding line: 2\n# Actual: First binding line: 3, Second binding line: 1\n```\n\nThe issue affects any .env file with multiple lines. Line numbers are being reported incorrectly, which breaks error reporting and debugging functionality that relies on accurate position information."
  }
